"The Ring", "Polygon", "Thomas", "Rose", "Los Angeles", "Butler", "America", "Disney Plus", "Hulu", "Freevee", "Henry", "Greek mythology", "AIDS", "London", "TBS", "Squid Game", "Betty", "The Exorcist", "William Peter Blatty", "Max", "Paramount Plus", "horror", "Criterion Channel", "Pete Volk", "Sam Raimi", "Kanopy", "Austen Goslin", "horror movies", "body horror", "Cure", "Kiyoshi Kurosawa", "Eyes Without a Face", "Georges Franju", "Prime Video", "Shudder", "Hoopla", "Song Kang-ho", "John Carpenter", "love", "Matt Patches", "Stephen King", "George A. Romero", "Peacock", "zombies", "AMC Plus", "Dario Argento", "The Texas Chain Saw Massacre", "Tobe Hooper", "Olivia Rodrigo", "World War II", "Nazis", "Ring", "Lovecraft", "Josh Ruben", "Hot Topic", "Petrana Radulovic", "internet", "Tech companies", "What to Watch"], "page": "The Halloween Countdown: 31 days of horror to watch (Polygon, 2023-10-10T15:27:53+00:00)", "passage": "The Halloween Countdown: 31 days of horror to watch (Polygon, 2023-10-10T15:27:53+00:00)\nLovecraft and the anti-consumerist allegories of George A. Romero. The horrors hold up over 50 years after it was first released, and with just the right combination of inadvertent silliness and legitimate terror, Messiah of Evil is a satisfying watch and an excellent start to a month of horrors. —Toussaint Egan\n\nOct. 2: Ginger Snaps\n\nWhere to watch: Criterion Channel, Shudder, Peacock, Vudu, Tubi, Freevee, Plex\n\nThere’s a sizable hole in the monster movie canon: There just aren’t enough good werewolf movies! Ginger Snaps is here to fix that. And if you love Jennifer’s Body, you’re in for a bloody treat.\n\nDirected by future Orphan Black co-creator John Fawcett, Ginger Snaps is a delightfully gruesome story about two sisters. One of them has gotten her period for the first time, and is turned into a werewolf shortly after. Things get messy, fast."}
