"The Ring", "Polygon", "Thomas", "Rose", "Los Angeles", "Butler", "America", "Disney Plus", "Hulu", "Freevee", "Henry", "Greek mythology", "AIDS", "London", "TBS", "Squid Game", "Betty", "The Exorcist", "William Peter Blatty", "Max", "Paramount Plus", "horror", "Criterion Channel", "Pete Volk", "Sam Raimi", "Kanopy", "Austen Goslin", "horror movies", "body horror", "Cure", "Kiyoshi Kurosawa", "Eyes Without a Face", "Georges Franju", "Prime Video", "Shudder", "Hoopla", "Song Kang-ho", "John Carpenter", "love", "Matt Patches", "Stephen King", "George A. Romero", "Peacock", "zombies", "AMC Plus", "Dario Argento", "The Texas Chain Saw Massacre", "Tobe Hooper", "Olivia Rodrigo", "World War II", "Nazis", "Ring", "Lovecraft", "Josh Ruben", "Hot Topic", "Petrana Radulovic", "internet", "Tech companies", "What to Watch"], "page": "The Halloween Countdown: 31 days of horror to watch (Polygon, 2023-10-10T15:27:53+00:00)", "passage": "The Halloween Countdown: 31 days of horror to watch (Polygon, 2023-10-10T15:27:53+00:00)\nThings get messy, fast.\n\nGinger Snaps doesn’t just do a great job filling in the werewolf canon. It’s a grisly body horror story placed onto an effective puberty allegory, with a compelling central sister relationship. If you’ve ever watched something like Sam Raimi’s Spider-Man and thought, This is great and surprisingly gooey, but give me stories like this about teen girls, then Ginger Snaps is for you.\n\nThe movie has amassed a dedicated cult following in the years since its release. You’re next up to join the ranks — see you at the next full moon! —Pete Volk\n\nOct. 3: Creepshow\n\nWhere to watch: Kanopy\n\nThe new Creepshow home video release — presented in vibrant 4K UHD Blu-ray — is the best way to revisit this horror anthology classic. You can see individual bubbles in the foam of the ocean as it slowly drowns Ted Danson. This is why it made our list of the best Blu-rays of 2023."}
